  "notes": "The priest's Communion under the species of wine: three psalm verses from two psalms — two of Psalm 115 said while he gathers the fragments, then Psalm 17, 4 — and the form said as he signs himself with the chalice. RETRÍBUAM at w002 has a form shared by the future indicative and present subjunctive. This edition reads the deliberative subjunctive: the interrogative QUID asks what the speaker is to render, and the following futures ACCÍPIAM and INVOCÁBO answer that question. RETRÍBUIT at w007 is likewise both present and perfect in form; there the sense decides, since the benefits asked about are ones already received, and the corpus claims the perfect. SALUTÁRIS at w010 is the genitive of the neuter noun salutáre, not the adjective — the chalice OF SALVATION, as the corpus already reads it at ordinarium.offerimus-tibi w005. SALVUS at w023 is confirmed by both analyzers, since Collatinus heads the word under its archaic nominative saluos, which the u/v folding cannot reach on its own; the pipeline now carries the alias, and the two votes agree.",
